## 1. Primary Request and Intent

The session began with a single bug report and evolved through many rounds of debugging, hardening, and reflection, ending in an explicit two-phase request that is the immediate active work:

- **Immediate, most recent request** (verbatim): *"This sounds a lot more sensible. Let's scope it our and prepare a fix please. Once done do a very deep analysis and thorough check of the code for similar mistakes we've made. Places where the exact same thing is implemented twice and places where we're complicating things unecessary. Use agent teams that are very targeted at identifying these types of issues. Then bring those back and analyze patterns and consider our overall architecture along with semantic models to propose comprehensive fixes that consider the whole vs just the issue one at a time. Present the findings and proposals."*
  - This has two phases: (A) implement the "persist-and-verify" redesign of release-commit decision verification (currently in progress), (B) after A is done, run a deep multi-agent audit of the whole codebase for (i) duplicate/parallel implementations of the same logic (drift risk) and (ii) unnecessary complexity, then synthesize architectural findings and present a comprehensive proposal.
- Earlier requests, all substantially completed: fix the release-PR camelCase serialization bug (PR #47, merged); harden the release-PR action's test suite to use the real binary, not stubs; migrate the release-PR executor from `git push` to GitHub's forge commit API (PR #49, merged) to avoid the `GITHUB_TOKEN` `.github/workflows/*` write restriction on public repos; fix a stuck release by reverting an unsigned merge (PR #50) and disabling rebase-merge repo-wide (squash-only enforced via `gh api -X PATCH`); clean up "AI slop" wording in workflow/spec files (PR #52, Tier 1 applied; Tier 2 spec-ID migration paused mid-discussion); fix a fixed-group cascade-authorization bug in `derive_release_commit_decision` (PR #53, opened but about to be superseded); set up a permission allowlist in `.claude/settings.json`; clean up the user's real local repo (`~/Projects/callisto`) to be on `main` with only legitimate changes.
